  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Temple Guide Page_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cc81bc5566bba4d10ba99c2c92ea3270, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 12922779590656
    m_Localized: "<b>\u2018Nippanassa Sacchikiriyaya Etangkasavang Kahetva\u2019\n\u2018I
      accept the saffron robe to realize Nirvana.\u2019</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18416499941376
    m_Localized: "<b>04:00 a.m.</b> Take up meditation practice <i>(mandatory activity)</i>\n\n<b>05:00
      a.m.</b> Morning chanting <i>(mandatory activity)</i>\n\n<b>06:00 a.m.</b>
      Monks go on alms round; laypeople prepare to offer alms or sweep leaves as
      a devotional act\n\n<b>07:00 a.m.</b> Mindful breakfast, silence observed in
      the dining hall, self-service and self-cleaning <i>(mandatory activity)</i>\n\n<b>09:00
      a.m.</b> Walking meditation (large area) <i>(mandatory activity)</i> followed
      by cleaning up the walking meditation area\n\n<b>10:00 a.m.</b> Audio teaching
      broadcast\n\n<b>11:00 a.m.</b> Monks\u2019 midday meal (lay practitioners may
      purchase meals at the temple shop for lunch and dinner)\n\n<b>12:00 p.m.</b>
      Insight meditation training, practicing psychic ability <i>(mandatory activity)</i>\n\n<b>01:30
      p.m.</b> Meditation review with the teacher, merit-making as desired, audio
      chanting broadcast\n\n<b>03:00 p.m.</b> Walking meditation practice <i>(mandatory
      activity)</i>\n\n<b>04:00 p.m.</b> Listen to teachings of Luang Por Ruesi on
      monastic discipline; sweep leaves as a devotional act\n\n<b>05:30 p.m.</b>
      Bell rings, prepare to assemble\n\n<b>06:00 p.m.</b> Evening chanting, take
      up meditation practice <i>(mandatory activity)</i>\n\n<b>08:00 p.m.</b> Free
      time for personal practice within the center\u2019s rules"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 20210252767232
    m_Localized: <b>(Refrain from using phones to avoid disturbance and prepare to
      wake up early)</b>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 14051038978048
    m_Localized: Wat Khao Wong (Narai Cave)
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27383554048
    m_Localized: "Laypeople and fellow monks and novices, everyone who comes to practice
      Dhamma at this temple does so with good intentions. That is, each person aspires
      toward Nirvana. In practicing goodness within the Buddha\u2019s teachings,
      especially for monks and novices, do not forget the word:"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 12979750821888
    m_Localized: "We aim to cultivate right view (samma-ditthi) and to follow the
      rules and discipline accurately. We practice what is good. Beyond that\u2026
      we reflect on the fact that birth, aging, illness, and death are undesirable
      and sources of suffering. We do not wish to be reborn; we seek only Nirvana.
      We resolve to give generously to cut through greed, to observe precepts to
      guard against anger, and to practice calm and insight meditation to eliminate
      delusion. We are determined to fulfill the Four Divine Abodes (Brahmaviharas)
      as follows:"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13053184696320
    m_Localized: '1. In terms of loving-kindness, we will love others as we love
      our own life, fostering a calm heart.

      2. Compassion will be a constant
      attitude. If it is within our capacity, we will help others find happiness
      to the best of our ability.

      3. We will not feel jealousy toward anyone.
      When others experience success, we will rejoice in their happiness.

      4.
      If someone makes a mistake and faces punishment or is cast out, and we are
      unable to help, we will remain neutral without adding to their burden.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17305286205440
    m_Localized: "This is the mindset we encourage for everyone here; both resident
      monks and novices, as well as those here for temporary practice. Let this be
      the guiding principle. First and foremost, please follow the temple\u2019s
      rules and customs as follows:"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17444017004544
    m_Localized: Daily Routine
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17317244166144
    m_Localized: 'Laypeople who come to Wat Khao Wong to practice Dhamma and meditation,
      and to live together in harmony, are kindly requested to observe the following:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17421782999040
    m_Localized: "1. When staying for Dhamma practice, you must uphold the Five or
      Eight Precepts completely, including the Ten Paths of Wholesome Action.*\n2.
      Everyone must participate in the temple\u2019s daily routines. The details
      of these routines are as follows:"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 20771102515200
    m_Localized: "<u><b>The Ten Paths of Wholesome Action*</b></u>\n\n1. Do not kill
      or harm animals, avoiding causing them suffering.\n2. Do not steal, which means
      not taking others\u2019 belongings without their willing consent.\n3. Do not
      commit adultery with the children, wives, or husbands of others. <i>(Additionally,
      avoid consuming alcohol and intoxicants that impair mindfulness)</i>\n4. Do
      not speak untruthfully.\n5. Do not speak harshly, avoiding words that cause
      distress to listeners.\n6. Do not speak divisively, refraining from words that
      create discord among others.\n7. Do not engage in idle or meaningless chatter.\n8.
      Do not covet others' belongings that the owner has not offered.\n9. Do not
      harbor ill will or malicious thoughts with the intent to harm anyone.\n10.
      Have faith in the Buddha and sincerely follow his teachings."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22248428658688
    m_Localized: "Everyone should regularly participate in meditation practice. Do
      not stay in your room during scheduled activities, as some may use this as
      an opportunity for personal gain\u2014when others are absent from their rooms,
      items may be stolen. If you come here with good intentions, join the meditation
      practice. If you are unable to participate due to any difficulty, please inform
      the staff at the abbot\u2019s office in advance."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22259262545920
    m_Localized: 3. If you wish to maintain a calm and relaxed state of mind while
      practicing Dhamma, we invite you to assist with small tasks around the temple,
      such as sweeping the temple grounds. This helps refresh your posture and brings
      a comfortable sense of focus. Ideally, everyone should help sweep the grounds
      as a way of giving back to the place that supports your practice. This is a
      tradition for practitioners at this center.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22350417354752
    m_Localized: Use of the Premises
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22745248161792
    m_Localized: 'The temple does not have sufficient staff to fully accommodate
      everyone. Therefore, we kindly ask for compassion from all laypeople to assist
      themselves and support the temple as follows:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22792073371648
    m_Localized: "1. Registration is open daily from 9:00 AM to 4:00 PM. Please bring
      a <b>National ID card</b> or <b>Government ID card</b> to register for a meditation
      retreat each time! <color=red>If you do not have the required ID with you,
      as stipulated by law, you will not be able to register or access this facility.</color>\n\n2.
      <b>The meditation retreat stay is limited to a maximum of 7 days per session.</b>\n\n3.
      Participation in activities and daily routines as designated by the temple
      is mandatory. Do not engage in any other activities outside those set by the
      temple\u2019s guidelines. <b>During activities, refrain from using communication
      devices. Please place them in containers provided by the staff, and collect
      them after the activities are complete.</b>\n\n4. If you need to leave the
      temple premises during the meditation retreat, please inform the staff at the
      main office and record each entry and exit in the logbook.\n\n5. Maintain restraint
      in body, speech, and mind, remembering that you are here to practice meditation.
      Do not disturb others by speaking loudly, lead others to other centers, solicit
      donations, or preach uninvited. Please come solely for meditation practice
      for personal purity and peace.\n\n6. When free from group activities, separate
      and meditate quietly. Do not gather in groups to chat, or engage in fortune-telling,
      healing, or mediumship in any form.\n\n7. Help maintain cleanliness in your
      room and surrounding areas. Everyone should assist with sweeping the temple
      grounds, which is the tradition and etiquette for residents in this Buddhist
      sanctuary.\n\n8. <b>The temple provides one meal per day.</b> If you wish for
      additional meals at noon or in the evening, the temple shop \u2018Wan Yang
      Kham\u2019 is open daily from 6:00 AM to 5:00 PM. <color=red>Do not bring food,
      snacks, or beverages to the accommodations</color> (drinking water is allowed).\n\n9.
      You may bring personal clothing to use in your room, but when outside, <b>you
      must wear the 'Khau Kan Bat' meditation attire</b> to distinguish practitioners
      from tourists. This attire is available for purchase at the temple's Wan Yang
      Kham shop (it can be worn on future visits). Pants/skirts should be in polite
      colors and styles, not short or tight-fitting (a specific white uniform is
      not required). <b>Jeans or clothing that may confuse practitioners with outsiders
      are not allowed.</b>\n   <color=red>Bring enough clothing and personal items
      for the duration of your stay. There are no facilities for washing and drying
      clothes.</color>\n\n10. This is a <b>\u2018Drug and Pet-Free Temple\u2019</b>.
      Smoking and all forms of substance abuse are prohibited. No pets, such as dogs
      or cats, are allowed within the temple premises <color=red>under any circumstances</color>.
      If you have pets with you (e.g., for a religious service), they must stay in
      your vehicle and are not allowed to roam or relieve themselves in the temple
      grounds. <color=red>Smoking is strictly prohibited on temple grounds, except
      in the designated smoking area!</color>\n\n11. This temple does not discriminate
      based on religious or political beliefs. We seek only peace here, so avoid
      discussing any topics that could lead to arguments or disputes.\n\n12. <b>This
      religious site is not a place for personal gain. Discussions, business dealings,
      or other matters that may lead to conflicts or fraud, such as business investment
      solicitations, debt collection, or profit collection, are not permitted.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22804677255168
    m_Localized: The above regulation is merely a recommendation to help you prepare
      yourself, both mentally and physically, appropriately. There are additional
      etiquette and traditions of the monastery that you must follow for your own
      well-being and for the well-being of others sharing the time and space. You
      will learn the details of these upon your arrival at Wat Khao Wong.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 190623435972608
    m_Localized: etiquette and traditions
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 190908334071808
    m_Localized: "1. When leaving the temple grounds or returning home, please inform
      the staff at the central office every time!\n   <b>Return keys and accommodation
      items and retrieve your card between 8:30 AM and 4:00 PM.</b>\n\n2. Do not
      act as a fortune-teller, perform mediumship, or engage in any similar practices
      under any circumstances.\n\n3. Do not engage in or request any healing, exorcism,
      or rituals by claiming any special or supernatural powers.\n\n4. Teachers or
      meditation instructors of this place must be certified and appointed by the
      abbot and the temple committee. They must guide students according to the teachings
      of the venerable Luang Por Reusi of Wat Tha Sung (Phra Rajphromyan) and must
      not encourage attachment to mystical powers or other realms beyond the present.
      The teachings should focus on abandoning all attachments to rebirth and cultivating
      the essence of Buddhism, which is:\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 191037950648320
    m_Localized: "\u2022 Encourage each other to abandon wrongdoing.\n\u2022 Encourage
      each other to do good according to the traditions of the monastery.\n\u2022
      Cultivate a mind that is bright, joyful, and firmly aspires to Nirvana as the
      ultimate goal."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 191043340328960
    m_Localized: '5. No selling or consumption of alcoholic beverages within the
      temple grounds. No bringing alcohol or intoxicants from outside into the temple.
      Violations are subject to legal penalties, including imprisonment for up to
      6 months and a fine not exceeding 10,000 Baht.


      6. No selling or using
      drugs or any kind of intoxicating substances within the temple grounds.


      7.
      No gambling of any kind within the temple grounds <i>(including all forms of
      lottery trading)</i>.


      8. No displaying of romantic behavior, whether
      subtle or overt, under any circumstances, even between spouses. Once entering
      the temple, self-restraint must be maintained.


      9. Individuals within
      this monastery, both residents and those here for meditation practice, must
      not engage in conversations or discussions that conflict with the monastery''s
      practices. Do not bring external issues into the monastery in the manner of
      <i>''fire outside, fire inside''</i>, and do not participate in activities
      not organized by the monastery.


      10. <b>Chanting the daily prayers</b>
      should be done by listening and following the lead of the monk in charge of
      the chanting, not according to one''s own habit <color=red>or chanting loudly
      as one wishes</color>.


      11. <b>Turn off all communication devices</b>
      when participating in activities and meditation practice <b>every time</b>
      <i>(they should be left with the instructor)</i>.


      12. If any action
      arises that leads to an investigation by the staff or the temple committee,
      <color=red>you must cooperate and follow the instructions without resistance</color>.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
